  "policy_prompt_for_action": [
    {
      "modify_from": "For each color, compute its completed count from its incoming deposited_<color> memory plus only that color's release visibly completed in the current incoming motion, exactly once, as in the memory update.",
      "modify_to": "For each color, compute its completed count from its incoming deposited_<color> memory plus only that color's newly completed release in the current incoming motion, exactly once, using the memory instruction's sparse-frame evidence test. A carried cube followed by an empty open hand, or a cube visibly separating or falling from the fingers over the opening followed by an empty open hand, can establish the release without a sampled finger-opening transition."
    },
    {
      "modify_from": "Cubes are approximately 4 cm wide: back-project their top-face centers at approximately z=0.04 and use the resulting world xy for the z=0.02 grasp.",
      "modify_to": "Cubes are approximately 4 cm wide: identify and back-project their top-face centers at approximately z=0.04 and use the resulting world xy for approach and the z=0.02 grasp. Use the top face, not the whole visible silhouette; visible side faces must not bias the center."
    },
    {
      "modify_from": "Locate the bin opening's geometric center from its elevated rim and opposing edges, checking both current views. Under partial occlusion, fit the opening geometry from visible rim segments and the other view; do not use the centroid of the visible dark fragment or intersect the opening center with the tabletop. Establish the opening reference height from observed geometry, not an assumed numeric rim height.",
      "modify_to": "Reconstruct the bin's rectangular inner opening from calibrated current front and wrist views. Identify corresponding inner-rim corners or edge intersections. For each image point [u,v,1], form a world ray with camera center C=-R^T t and direction d=R^T K^-1[u,v,1], using that camera's current calibration. Triangulate reliable corresponding rim points and fit their common horizontal plane. Fit the rectangular inner opening to visible opposing edges in that plane; reconstruct occluded corners from the fitted edges rather than using the centroid of the visible dark fragment. Compute the world center from opposing corners or edge midlines, and check that the fitted opening reprojects onto visible rim segments in both views. Do not average image centroids across cameras, use occluding silhouette boundaries as rim correspondences, or intersect the opening center with the tabletop. If reliable reconstruction is unavailable, use the purposeful visibility-recovery motion below rather than inventing a rim height. Use this same geometrically defined center for closed transfer and separate release at z=0.20 and for retreat at [bin_x-0.10,bin_y,0.20]."
    },
    {
      "modify_from": "When already above that cube near z=0.15, descend to its center at z=0.02 and close. Use the wrist view to refine the same cube's center rather than descending at an inaccurate reported approach position.",
      "modify_to": "When already above an eligible cube near z=0.15, identify the approached cube by projecting [current_tcp_x,current_tcp_y,0.04] into the current wrist image with its calibration. Identify the eligible top face nearest that projection, cross-checking world-space proximity and the incoming approach frames. Neither the wrist image center nor the largest visible cube is the alignment reference. Refine that same cube's top-face center at approximately z=0.04, then descend at its world xy to z=0.02 and close, preserving the approached cube's edge-aligned orientation. Do not switch to another prominent cube or descend at an inaccurate measured approach xy."
    },
    {
      "modify_from": "The target is the opening center, not the measured TCP xy. Opening remains a separate operation from the closed-hand transfer. Add a 0.003 m vertical displacement only if the centered target would otherwise produce no motion.",
      "modify_to": "The target is the opening center, not the measured TCP xy. Opening remains a separate operation from the closed-hand transfer. Correct both lateral coordinates before testing whether the centered target would produce no motion; add a 0.003 m vertical displacement only in that case."
    },
    {
      "modify_from": "When already aligned above the button with open fingers, close the empty gripper at that approach position, adding a 0.003 m vertical displacement if needed to ensure a nonzero motion.",
      "modify_to": "When already aligned above the button with open fingers, re-localize the gray circular button-top center, back-projecting it at approximately z=0.02 and checking the other current view when visible. Use the circular top, not the surrounding square base. Command [button_x,button_y,0.15,-3.1416,0,0] and close the empty gripper. Correct the target before testing the nonzero-motion requirement; add a 0.003 m vertical displacement only if the corrected target would otherwise produce no motion."
    }
  ],
  "refused": "No fixed color priority, nearest-hand or nearest-robot rule, image-position preference, or scene-specific target list is added. Neither round establishes a consistent tie-breaker among multiple eligible, accessible, unaligned cubes, and future recorded selections cannot supply predictable memory. That exact new-target selection ambiguity remains unresolved. No new memory field, stored bin position, assumed numeric rim height, or annotation change is justified. Earlier per-color counts, aligned-target persistence, separate transfer and release, bin-relative mandatory retreat, and unrestricted feasible edge-aligned yaw remain intact."
}
